{"body":"## 🤖 AI-Powered Solution Draft\n\nThis pull request is being automatically generated to solve issue #2625.\n\n### 📋 Issue Reference\nFixes #2625\n\n### 🚧 Status\n**Work in Progress** - The AI assistant is currently analyzing and implementing the solution draft.\n\n### 📝 Implementation Details\n_Details will be added as the solution draft is developed..._\n\n---\n*This PR was created automatically by the AI issue solver*","commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-10-07T13:30:42Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-07T13:30:42Z","messageBody":"Adding .gitkeep for PR creation (default mode).\nThis file will be removed when the task is complete.\n\nIssue: https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2625","messageHeadline":"Initial commit with task details","oid":"f7fa845fa51d9935cca703593a3a316190973a2f"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-07T13:38:39Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-07T13:38:39Z","messageBody":"… failure reason\n\ngh api user returns HTTP 403 'Resource not accessible by integration' for\nGITHUB_TOKEN; verifyResults threw on it and the catch printed an empty\nreason because the message was passed as log()'s options argument.\n\nRefs #2625","messageHeadline":"fix(solve): verify results with integration tokens and print the real…","oid":"00973d16ce8de11377acefff618a3416c7f5c744"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-07T13:40:25Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-07T13:40:25Z","messageBody":"The dependency-freshness gate failed every main push since command-stream\n2.0.0 (Node >= 22) was published, skipping lint, tests and the release.\n\nRefs #2625","messageHeadline":"chore(deps): bump command-stream to 2.0.0 and Sentry to 11.5.0","oid":"44081ee5b8fbc5cc76511cd55392fe40ef81619f"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-07T13:41:59Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-07T13:41:59Z","messageBody":"… only\n\nA release published after a merge failed detect-changes on the push to main\nand skipped lint, tests, the release, Docker and Helm (runs 37577002856,\n37603761465, 37603921340). Non-PR events now warn with annotations and a step\nsummary; pull requests stay fail-closed as issue #2264 requires.\n\nRefs #2625","messageHeadline":"fix(ci): keep the dependency-freshness gate blocking on pull requests…","oid":"9ebc0ce5c719bd812f90758df3a1fc894fb3cbe6"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-07T13:53:33Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-07T13:53:33Z","messageBody":"…anup errors\n\nRuleset 21204104 forbids deleting any branch and nobody can bypass it, so\nevery DELETE in the daily cleanup answered HTTP 422 and the job failed every\nday since 2026-10-03. The cleanup now asks the rules API first, classifies a\nrule violation on DELETE the same way the E2E cleanup does, reports one\nwarning per run and fails only on real errors. The misleading 'scheduled\ncleanup will retry' message now names what is required.\n\nRefs #2625","messageHeadline":"fix(ci): treat ruleset-retained fixture branches as retained, not cle…","oid":"407da13b0acd410b949f14ac615b0ef1233043fe"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-07T14:05:27Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-07T14:05:27Z","messageBody":"OpenCode Zen withdrew nemotron-3-super-free (link-assistant/agent#327), so\nthe E2E row agent / nemotron-3-super-free (run 37616874265) failed with\n'Model \"nemotron-3-super-free\" not found in provider \"opencode\"'. Zen's\nremaining free models answer HTTP 403 FreeTierError to non-OpenCode\nclients, so the default now maps to kilo/nemotron-3-super-free and Hive\nMind supplies the provider entry Agent 0.26.11 lacks through\nLINK_ASSISTANT_AGENT_CONFIG_CONTENT, both for the connection check and\nfor the task run. A user definition of the same model wins.\n\nRefs #2625","messageHeadline":"fix(agent): run the default free model on the Kilo gateway","oid":"e6d2555ba7a59f713c0b9e8e4eae6088f7fd0931"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-07T14:05:31Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-07T14:05:31Z","messageBody":"Refs #2625","messageHeadline":"docs: document the Kilo gateway default free model","oid":"4a75d9ff19ea8ae4d4e3db0b657ec678c74b1dc2"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-07T14:05:37Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-07T14:05:37Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"chore(issue-2625): keep the Agent provider smoke test and its evidence","oid":"7cd1309dd3e2c88239ec65c0e565e39167c5cf48"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-07T14:05:56Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-07T14:05:56Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"chore(issue-2625): collect CI logs and repository data for the analysis","oid":"448c384fd179541251a4cdc5baa515e17733290a"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-07T14:12:48Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-07T14:12:48Z","messageBody":"solve opened its log in the working directory before parsing argv and never\nmoved it, so --log-dir was a no-op. The Formal AI Draft workflow bind-mounts\n--log-dir out of its container; every run since #2233 uploaded an empty\ndirectory ('No files were found with the provided path'). The log is now\ncopied into --log-dir right after parsing (rename fails with EXDEV across a\nbind mount) and later writes go there.\n\nRefs #2625","messageHeadline":"fix(solve): apply --log-dir to the session log","oid":"47781dd1eee4ac0ff20c291b7b8e8d61917f41ab"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-07T14:13:51Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-07T14:13:51Z","messageBody":"bump_type was required without a default, so GitHub refused the checks\ndispatch of every Formal AI draft with HTTP 422 \"Required input\n'bump_type' not provided\"; no such dispatch has ever started. patch is\nwhat the web form already preselects.\n\nRefs #2625","messageHeadline":"fix(ci): let release.yml be dispatched with only mode=checks","oid":"e602cc324056240b5ffcab9e85f64d65ba7968c1"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-07T14:15:59Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-07T14:15:59Z","messageBody":"A workflow GITHUB_TOKEN gets HTTP 403 'Resource not accessible by\nintegration' from POST /gists. The upload retried after 30s and 2m and\nthen re-sent the log as parts, all failing identically (Formal AI Draft\nrun 37606848542). Permission refusals now end the upload on the first\nattempt; secondary rate limits keep their retries.\n\nRefs #2625","messageHeadline":"fix(attach-logs): do not retry a token that cannot create gists","oid":"b7fbf5e76aa1aab5cd194b49b8db4413b68d40e6"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-07T14:18:59Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-07T14:18:59Z","messageBody":"gh pr edit --add-label formal-ai-draft failed with \"'formal-ai-draft'\nnot found\" (run 37606848542): the repository never had the label, so\nno draft was ever labelled. The workflow now creates it (without\n--force, so a customised label is kept) and labels again.\n\nRefs #2625","messageHeadline":"fix(formal-ai-draft): create the draft label when it is missing","oid":"982dbee6ae4478a397795145ccf1df5808d77dac"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-07T14:20:07Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-07T14:20:07Z","messageBody":"Full logs of the failing runs and every Formal AI Draft run since\n2026-10-03, fetched from the jobs API because gh run view --log\ntruncates. Presigned S3 credentials in the logs are redacted.\n\nRefs #2625","messageHeadline":"chore(issue-2625): keep the full CI job logs as evidence","oid":"85521438e557815de2f20af102f2069d38b576f2"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-07T14:23:04Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-07T14:23:04Z","messageBody":"Refs #2625","messageHeadline":"chore(issue-2625): reproduce Formal AI reading 'e.g' as a file","oid":"2981093a13c4e423277d71101378cde43afee325"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-07T14:28:57Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-07T14:28:57Z","messageBody":"…world\n\nRecords the four false negatives issue #2625 found on main: an external-state\ngate that failed pushes, policy refusals that were retried or failed daily, a\nrequired dispatch input without a default, a label the run assumed existed,\nand a log written where the upload never looked. Pinned in en/hi/ru/zh.\n\nRefs #2625","messageHeadline":"docs(ci-cd): add principle 17, tell a broken pipeline from a changed …","oid":"d5cd3300e32906026383e95a0d9352de58e4687c"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-07T14:29:00Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-07T14:29:00Z","messageBody":"…ison evidence\n\nRefs #2625","messageHeadline":"chore(issue-2625): keep the template release-preflight logs as compar…","oid":"2671be6b3aa1fc85d0a22f0e9856ed5524ccbda7"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-07T14:29:06Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-07T14:29:06Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"chore(changeset): patch release for issue #2625 CI/CD fixes","oid":"fe9650ea5c8f20cf12b64ef0da951e9ce35ba649"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-07T14:31:46Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-07T14:31:46Z","messageBody":"…stream reports\n\nRefs #2625","messageHeadline":"docs(issue-2625): case study with timeline, root causes, fixes and up…","oid":"d5b9a2bff3bf5ba7e442ed084c1a8491b6429601"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-07T14:35:58Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-07T14:35:58Z","messageBody":"Refs #2625","messageHeadline":"style(agent): keep agent.lib.mjs within the 1350-line warning threshold","oid":"577c927c5651ddc8b29173d6975234ab8127010e"}],"files":[{"path":".changeset/ci-false-negatives-2625.md","additions":5,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":".github/workflows/release.yml","additions":8,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"README.hi.md","additions":1,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"README.md","additions":1,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"README.ru.md","additions":1,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"README.zh.md","additions":1,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"dev/log/issues/2625/pulls/2626/README.md","additions":141,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"dev/log/issues/2625/pulls/2626/ci-logs/formal-ai-draft/run-37126292445-job-111212121275.log","additions":283,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"dev/log/issues/2625/pulls/2626/ci-logs/formal-ai-draft/run-37204604042-job-111443069298.log","additions":4355,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"},{"path":"dev/log/issues/2625/pulls/2626/ci-logs/formal-ai-draft/run-37237191915-job-111538571256.log","a